  """
  Create an asynchronous stream

  \brief Create an asynchronous stream

  Creates a new asynchronous stream on the context that is current to the calling host thread. If no context is current to the calling host thread, then the primary context for a device is selected, made current to the calling thread, and initialized before creating a stream on it. The \p flags argument determines the behaviors of the stream.  Valid values for \p flags are - ::cudaStreamDefault: Default stream creation flag. - ::cudaStreamNonBlocking: Specifies that work running in the created stream may run concurrently with work in stream 0 (the NULL stream), and that the created stream should perform no implicit synchronization with stream 0.

  \param pStream - Pointer to new stream identifier \param flags   - Parameters for stream creation

